WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:05.640
After Natalie Portman was revealed at Comic-Con
2019 to be taking the mantle of Thor in the

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:09.830
upcoming Thor: Love and Thunder, artists began
imagining what she would look like when she

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:11.980
transforms into the Goddess of Thunder.

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:15.680
Here are what a few fans thought the actress
could look like as the Mighty Thor.

00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:21.620
Artist Pablo Ruiz, who goes by the handle
@pabloruizzx on Instagram, envisioned Natalie

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:25.640
Portman's Mighty Thor as a companion to Chris
Hemsworth's Asgardian God of Thunder.

00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:30.680
Holding the mystical hammer Mjolnir in her
hand, with her eyes glowing blue, Jane-as-Thor

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:33.260
stands behind the Odinson as he reaches back
for her help.

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:38.710
It appears that @pabloruizzx used a Jane Foster
Sideshow Collectibles figure designed by Ian

00:00:38.710 --> 00:00:41.820
MacDonald and Alex Pascenko as the basis for
this edit.

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:46.900
Popular Australian artist Mizuri, who goes
by @mizuriofficial on Instagram, quickly shared

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:48.260
their vision of the Mighty Thor.

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:53.080
In their artwork, Natalie Portman's Jane Foster
wears armor, a dark red cape, and a helmet

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:55.740
evocative of the Jane Foster Thor from the
comics.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.899
Mizuri also posted an unmasked version of
the Jane Foster Thor edit, which uses a Thor:

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:05.520
The Dark World poster featuring Portman as
a starting point for these creative alterations.

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:09.679
Artist @doubledomino made a piece featuring
the Mighty Thor wearing her comic book headgear

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:11.560
surrounded by a storm of lightning.

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:16.460
Their artwork also uses the Thor: The Dark
World poster of Portman as a basis and uses

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:20.040
the Jane Foster Thor helmet design provided
by Do3D.com.

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:25.119
ALASTØR, a longtime comic book fan and art
director posting on Instagram under the username

00:01:25.119 --> 00:01:30.149
@alastor_c, predicted years ago that Natalie
Portman would eventually become the next Thor

00:01:30.149 --> 00:01:31.659
in the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:36.340
"You're--" "I'm Loki." * "That was for
New York."

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:38.560
"I like her!"

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:41.760
His idea for how the Jane Foster Thor could
look on screen?

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:47.579
She dons a red cape, wears a silver chest-plate,
and wields not one but two weapons — Mjolnir

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:49.679
and the Dwarven-forged battle axe Jarnbjorn.

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:54.539
It looks like @alastor_c used the Jane Foster
figure for a base and then Photoshopped Portman's

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:55.920
head in place of Jane's.

00:01:56.469 --> 00:02:01.279
Indonesian artist @awedope.arts uploaded a
striking image depicting Jane Foster and Thor

00:02:01.279 --> 00:02:05.849
Odinson standing side by side as if they're
about to partner up and take down a baddie

00:02:05.849 --> 00:02:06.380
together.

00:02:06.849 --> 00:02:10.959
While Odinson, his hair long and his beard
braided, holds his battle axe Stormbreaker

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:14.560
in both hands, a helmet-wearing Mighty Thor
carries Mjolnir.

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:18.840
Once again, it looks like the artwork makes
use of the Jane Foster figure as the basis

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:19.840
for the Mighty Thor.

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:25.860
Self-proclaimed "graphic wizard" Jakub Masłowski,
@jakubmaslowski_ on Instagram, imagined that

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:30.760
the Portman as Thor will sport a simpler look
in Thor: Love and Thunder, wearing the classic

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:32.940
costume fans saw in the first Thor film.

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:37.280
In Maslowski's artwork, Portman's Mighty Thor
wears the signature red cape, intricately

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:41.560
designed armor, and matching gauntlets originally
worn by Chris Hemsworth in Thor.

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:44.880
And, of course, she has the lightning-powered
Mjolnir in hand as well.

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:46.160
"Oh.

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:47.180
My.

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:48.780
God."

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:53.700
Natalie Portman's Mighty Thor could sport
an intense appearance in Thor: Love and Thunder,

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:57.400
if artist @ihasankazi's vision for the character
ends up being accurate.

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:01.680
In their artwork, the Mighty Thor has a heavier
costume and glowing blue eyes.

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:06.180
Instead of creating a Photoshop edit of what
Natalie Portman's Mighty Thor could look like

00:03:06.189 --> 00:03:11.030
in Thor: Love and Thunder, artist Nikolay
Mochkin, @ellejart on Instagram, created a

00:03:11.030 --> 00:03:12.969
complete illustration of the character.

00:03:12.969 --> 00:03:17.489
Here, Jane Foster is depicted taking to the
skies, her red cape flowing behind her and

00:03:17.489 --> 00:03:19.780
Mjolnir summoning the power of lightning up
above.

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:23.840
We'll just have to wait and see if Natalie
Portman's Mighty Thor looks like any of these

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:28.689
fantastic portrayals or instead ends up closer
to the look she had in the animated series

00:03:28.689 --> 00:03:29.920
Avengers Assemble.

